VERIFIED PARSER FACT, and the reason no keyword is added: Parse.$$$
needs its literal in the theory's keyword table, but Args.$$$
(Pure/Isar/args.ML:81) matches an IDENT *or* keyword token by content
and marks it Markup.quasi_keyword — no declaration required, jEdit
still highlights it. so enum, list, of, optional, annotations and
exactly_one are parsed with Args.$$$. declaring them in the MCP_Tools
header instead would be actively harmful: a minor keyword lexes as a
keyword token in EVERY importing theory, so "list" would break
"thm list.induct" and friends throughout MCP-HOL. "|" is already a Pure
quasi_command keyword, so enum items parse as Parse.enum1 "|"
Parse.name inside Parse.$$$ "(" ... ")" — the same tokens clause_block
already uses.

the ptyp parser is recursive ("list of list of string" parses; whether
it is USEFUL is a schema question, and the json mapping nests fine).
