spec refinements (fold back into the spec at step 7)
-----------------------------------------------------

- spec refinement: an enum value substitutes VERBATIM into the format,
  like args/fact and unlike string. the spec's quoting bullet does not
  say. rationale: enum items exist to name command keywords
  ("find_definition kind: const" breaks if quoted), and membership
  validation against a declaration-time set makes the splice safe where
  a free string would not be — which is why param also checks the items
  are token-safe.
- spec refinement: "list of <scalar>" joins with a SINGLE SPACE after
  per-element type-directed quoting. the spec says "space- or
  comma-joined per an optional join spec"; the join spec is DEFERRED
  (no declared user), one join rule ships.
- spec refinement: a List_Of param takes no "= default". a list-literal
  default syntax is not specced; rejected at registration, DEFERRED.
- spec refinement: an absent (optional) param substitutes the EMPTY
  STRING in the format. the spec says "omitted = absent from the
  format" / "omitted optionals erase their segment", which presupposes
  segment machinery that does not exist — $flag?text is specced and
  still unimplemented (scan_format knows only $name). segment erasure
